--------------------------------------------------------------------------

A note on what a licence can and cannot do here.

This game runs in a browser. Everything needed to play it is delivered to the
player's machine, and no technical measure changes that — a determined person
can always take a copy of what their own browser has already downloaded. What
this file does is remove any ambiguity about whether they are permitted to.
That is a legal protection rather than a technical one, and it is the only kind
that genuinely applies to a client-side game.

The technical measures that are worth having are in place and are aimed at the
things that are actually preventable: the build no longer ships source maps, so
the original TypeScript is not handed over; the site refuses to run inside
another page, so it cannot be framed and passed off as somebody else's; and the
response headers in public/_headers lock down what the page may load. See the
Security section of README.md.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Third-party components are used under their own licences and are not covered by
the above:

  three.js            MIT
  vite, esbuild,
  typescript          MIT

Map geometry under public/city/, where present, is derived from OpenStreetMap
data, © OpenStreetMap contributors, and is used under the Open Database Licence
(ODbL). The attribution this requires is displayed in-game.
